WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.710
Let’s talk about food, sleep, and recovery.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:08.520
Nourishment is about food and nutrition needs.

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:12.130
Food choices need to fit your own health and life.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:19.700
Food does not replace your prescribed PsA care, and no single food can switch off PsA.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:30.990
The source suggests meals built around color and protein: vegetables, fruit like berries or citrus, olive oil, and a good protein source.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.220
Use these as topics to discuss with your team.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:40.020
A dietitian can teach you about nutrition, and keeping a healthy weight.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:45.030
Ask before adding supplements, or making big diet changes.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:49.150
Repose is about rest and sleep.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:55.600
Pain or worry can make sleep harder, and poor sleep can make the next day’s pain feel worse.

00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:59.500
Good sleep helps your body recover.

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:03.160
Try to keep a steady time for bed, and for waking.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:09.340
A dark, cool room, and a calm wind-down routine, may help.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:14.610
Avoid late caffeine, alcohol, and heavy meals before bed.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:24.780
Bring ongoing sleep problems to your care team. Say if pain, waking at night, or daytime tiredness is the main problem.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:28.920
Ask for help, rather than changing your medicine on your own.

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:36.520
Meals, movement, coping, and rest should fit together, into a routine you can manage.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:40.590
Great job! Let’s review.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:44.490
Food does not replace your prescribed PsA care.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:47.860
Bring ongoing sleep problems to the care team.
